-- M3 fixes, A3 (C15): genuine run-mode prelude coverage.  Both
-- PASS-CHECK-PRELUDE and PASS-RUN-PRELUDE used to derive from the ONE
-- bootstrap-only exit code, which only proves `Bootstrap.state ()`
-- succeeds (a check-time operation).  This fixture makes the RUN
-- marker execute prelude code for real: `add` is a prelude
-- `reducible def rec`, applied here to canonical Nat data, so a green
-- gate proves Interp's exec/force/quote path works over a prelude rec
-- def in run mode.  dev/gates.sh pins the exact output line
-- `(succ (succ (succ zero)))`, a computed readback, never an echo.
eval add (succ (succ zero)) (succ zero)
